  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09GE">Example <span data-tag="09GE">9.8.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a compact Riemann surface, and let $f \in \mathbf{C}(X) - \mathbf{C}$ any nonconstant meromorphic function on $X$ (see Example <a href="/tag/09FL" data-tag="09FL">9.3.6</a>). Then it is known that $\mathbf{C}(X)$ is algebraic over the subextension $\mathbf{C}(f)$ generated by $f$. We shall not prove this. </p>
